---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";

const faqs = [
  {
    id: "what-is-the-amsterdam-pauper-league",
    title: "What is the Amsterdam Pauper League?",
    content: `<div class="space-y-4">
      <p>The Amsterdam Pauper League (APL) is a community of <a href="https://magic.wizards.com/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Magic: The Gathering</a> players dedicated to the <a href="https://magic.wizards.com/en/formats/pauper" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Pauper format</a>. We organise tournaments in Amsterdam and fly Dutch players to <a href="https://www.instagram.com/Paupergeddon.official" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Paupergeddon</a>, the largest Pauper event in the world.</p>
      <p>Founded in Amsterdam on June 6, 2026, the APL is part of the international network of Pauper leagues coordinated by <a href="https://www.facebook.com/legapauperitalia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Lega Pauper Italia</a> (LPI). We follow LPI's guidelines to organise our activities and deliver a rewarding Pauper experience to players in the Netherlands.</p>
      <p>The APL was born as the successor to the Dutch Pauper League.</p>
    </div>`,
  },
  {
    id: "what-about-the-dutch-pauper-league",
    title: "What about the Dutch Pauper League?",
    content: `<div class="space-y-4">
      <p>The Dutch Pauper League was born as the successor to the Amsterdam Pauper Series. It organised Pauper tournaments in Amsterdam from January 28, 2024 to June 6, 2026.</p>
      <p>LPI supported players during the transition from Dutch Pauper League to Amsterdam Pauper League by preserving standings points for the 2026 season.</p>
    </div>`,
  },
  {
    id: "how-can-i-participate",
    title: "How can I participate?",
    content: `<p>Join any leg, and you will become a member of the league. Each leg awards league points, and your final position in the season standings determines your knockout qualification and eligibility for Paupergeddon rewards, including byes and travel allowances.</p>`,
  },
  {
    id: "what-does-the-dpl-organise",
    title: "What does the APL organise?",
    content: `<div class="space-y-4">
      <p>Each year, the APL organises events at different Rules Enforcement Levels (RELs) to ensure the best environments for players of different skill levels:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Monthly <strong>legs</strong>. Single-day tournaments, open to everybody. Match results award leg prizes of the day and league points for the season standings. Each leg is a paid-entry Swiss tournament run under <a href="https://media.wizards.com/2022/wpn/marketing_materials/wpn/mtg_jar_25sep20_en.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Regular REL</a>.</li>
        <li>End-of-season <strong>knockout</strong>. A playoff for the top-ranked players to decide the league champion. The knockout is a free-entry tournament for qualified players only, run under <a href="https://media.wizards.com/ContentResources/WPN/MTG_MTR_2025_Apr%2021_EN.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Competitive REL</a>.</li>
        <li>Up to twice a year, an <strong>International Pauper Tour</strong> (IPT).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>`,
  },
  {
    id: "how-are-season-standings-calculated",
    title: "How are season standings calculated?",
    content: `<div class="space-y-4">
      <p>Points are awarded based on match outcomes: 3 points per win, 1 point per draw, 0 points per loss.</p>
      <p>Standings count each player's <strong>best 7 of 8 events</strong>. If a player has joined 7 or less events during a season, all of them are counted.</p>
    </div>`,
  },
  {
    id: "who-qualifies-for-the-knockout",
    title: "Who qualifies for the knockout?",
    content: `<p>After all season legs are played, the <strong>Top 8</strong> players in the standings qualify for the knockout. If there's a tie for the final spots, all tied players are invited.</p>`,
  },
  {
    id: "how-does-the-knockout-work",
    title: "How does the knockout work?",
    content: `<div class="space-y-4">
      <p>The knockout tournament consists of two stages:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>3-Round Swiss Stage</strong>. All qualified players compete in a three-round Swiss tournament to determine the Top 4.</li>
        <li><strong>Top 4 Playoff</strong>. The four highest-ranked players from the Swiss stage advance to a single-elimination bracket to decide the APL Champion of the season.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This format is suggested by LPI to ensure players compete in multiple matches, with the final rounds determining the overall winner.</p>
      <p>For every match, the starting player is decided randomly.</p>
    </div>`,
  },
  {
    id: "what-can-i-win",
    title: "What can I win?",
    content: `<div class="space-y-4">
      <p>The APL awards prizes at every level of play:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Leg prizes</strong>: awarded at each event, scaling with attendance.</li>
        <li><strong>League Standings Winner</strong>: the player with the most league points at the end of the season. Eligible for Paupergeddon travel allowance and bye based on attendance.</li>
        <li><strong>APL Champion</strong>: winner of the knockout. Represents the Netherlands at Paupergeddon with guaranteed travel allowance. Eligible for a bye based on attendance.</li>
        <li><strong>Knockout Runner-up</strong>: second place in the knockout. Eligible for Paupergeddon travel allowance and bye based on attendance.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>`,
  },
  {
    id: "how-does-store-credit-work",
    title: "How does store credit work?",
    content: `<div class="space-y-4">
      <p>The APL partners with the <a href="http://pauperformance.market/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Pauperformance Market</a> to handle prizes.</p>
      <p>The APL prizes are given as store credit spendable on the Pauperformance Market. The store credit you win is automatically credited to your personal account using the email associated with your TopDeck account. As the APL and Pauperformance Market are two separate entities, the responsibility to deliver prizes is entirely on the Pauperformance Market.</p>
      <p>You can spend your store credit on a wide variety of pauper cards, accessories, and APL merchandising according to availability. Additionaly, you can purchase APL entry tickets for the ongoing season. More information on prizes and terms of conditions are available on the <a href="https://pauperformance.market/faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Pauperformance Market FAQ</a>.</p>
    </div>`,
  },
  {
    id: "how-do-byes-and-travel-allowance-work",
    title: "How do byes and travel allowance work?",
    content: `<div class="space-y-4">
      <p>We aim to cover round-trip flights for eligible players. Byes for Paupergeddon depend on the average attendance of the <strong>7 largest legs</strong> in the year:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>16</strong>+ avg players: unlocks 1 bye for the APL Champion</li>
        <li><strong>32</strong>+ avg players: unlocks 1 additional bye for the Standings Winner and travel allowance</li>
        <li><strong>64</strong>+ avg players: unlocks 1 additional bye for the Knockout Runner-up and travel allowance</li>
      </ul>
    </div>`,
  },
  {
    id: "what-if-one-player-wins-both-titles",
    title: "What if one player wins both titles?",
    content: `<p>If one player wins both the standings and the knockout, the extra bye passes down to the next eligible knockout finisher.</p>`,
  },
  {
    id: "can-the-dpl-help-me-get-a-paupergeddon-ticket",
    title: "Can the APL help me get a Paupergeddon ticket?",
    content: `<p>Yes. As a league member, you can buy a pre-sale ticket directly from LPI. Contact us for details.</p>`,
  },
  {
    id: "when-does-the-season-reset",
    title: "When does the season reset?",
    content: `<p>After the knockout, the league standings are cleared, and the new season begins.</p>`,
  },
  {
    id: "whats-the-dpls-long-term-goal",
    title: "What's the APL's long-term goal?",
    content: `<p>Our aim is to consistently run 8 legs with 64+ players so three Dutch players each year get travel allowances and byes for Paupergeddon. That means raising the competitive level in the Netherlands and making sure talented players get the support they deserve.</p>`,
  },
];
---

<Layout title="FAQ – Amsterdam Pauper League">
  <main class="flex-1">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-screen-lg px-4 py-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tighter mb-2">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-8">
        Everything you need to know about the Amsterdam Pauper League.
      </p>

      {faqs.map(({ id, title, content }, index) => (
        <section id={id} class:list={["py-8 scroll-mt-20", index < faqs.length - 1 && "border-b border-border"]}>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 group">
            {title}<a href={`#${id}`} class="inline-block ml-2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary text-lg font-normal" aria-label="Link to section">#</a>
          </h2>
          <div class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed" set:html={content} />
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
